<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#old-high-german">Glossary</a> · Term · language</p><h1 class="enc-title">Old High German</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Old High German is the earliest recorded stage of the German language, used from about the eighth to the eleventh century. It was spoken in the eastern Frankish realm of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oaths-of-strasbourg">Oaths of Strasbourg</a> of 842 CE contain one of its earliest surviving texts, sworn by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-german">Louis the German</a>'s troops.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/old-high-german.jpg" alt="Old High German" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hildebrandslied_Teil_1_von_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
